<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via over-the-weekend system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via over-the-weekend system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added reserves into the banking system through a round of over-the-weekend system repurchase agreements Friday, said a New York Fed spokeswoman.</p>
<p>The operation was expected by the market. It follows overnight system RPs totalling $7.649 billion Thurdsay.</p>
<p>Federal funds were trading at the 5-1/4 percent target rate when the Fed entered the open market.</p>
<p>-- Steven Scheer, N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1867</p>
</text>
